The 0/1 Loss
A simple loss function could be the 0/1 loss, which is trivial in some sense. The 0/1 loss simply counts the number of misclassifications.

The 0/1 loss function for a single example is defined as: \[L_{0/1}(y, \hat{y}) = \begin{cases}
    0 & \text{if } y = \hat{y} \\
    1 & \text{if } y \neq \hat{y}
\end{cases}\] where \(y\) is the true label and \(\hat{y}\) is the predicted label. The total 0/1 loss over a dataset is the number of misclassifications.
